 ],
 "note": "r8 implementation change from #75 (which answers a worker backlog gap with a reload, then error and close): the worker's backlog dropped m-0005..m-0007 while the broker was busy. The host reloads the worker's history and sends what it recovered (m-0006, m-0007) as sequenced message{history: true} with after_message_id, in timeline order, then the live stream goes on. m-0005 is no longer in the worker's history either, so a coverage event reports a persistent hole between m-0004 and m-0006 inside the retained timeline (not truncation: oldest_retained is unchanged). No error, no close, no reopen loop; reopening shows the same hole, which nothing can repair."
}